# ── Third-party exam material ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `exam/` holds an authored IELTS package and `fixtures/exams/exam-1.json`
# plus its assets are what `scripts/import-exam-package.py` produces from it.
#
# Two reasons neither is committed, and the first is the one that matters:
# the package's own manifest records that the source material is watermarked
# "REAL IELTS TESTS" and linked to a Telegram channel, and that the right to
# use it is unestablished. Committing 22MB of media whose licence nobody has
# checked is not a decision to make by accident.
#
# Rebuild it locally with:
#   python3 scripts/import-exam-package.py exam/Exam1 exam-1
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing: `exam/` with no anchor matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, and it silently swallowed
# `apps/web/src/features/exam/` — the entire exam-taking UI. Already-tracked
# files there kept showing as modified, so the only symptom was three new
# components that never appeared in `git status`.
/exam/
/fixtures/exams/exam-1.json
/fixtures/exams/assets/exam-1-*

# ── Owner-supplied IELTS source material ──────────────────────────────────
#
# `Đề IELTS/` holds the Cambridge papers, the band calculator and the Writing
# and Speaking criteria the owner handed over. Same class as `/exam/` above and
# ignored for the same two reasons: nobody has established the right to
# redistribute it, and one file in there is a 1.3 GB archive that has no
# business in a git history whatever its licence turns out to be.
#
# It is also in `.prettierignore` — for a different failure. `prettier --check .`
# tried to read that archive into a string and died, taking the whole
# formatting gate with it.
/Đề IELTS/

# Playwright's own output. Traces are megabytes and are only useful on the
# machine that produced them.
e2e/test-results/
e2e/playwright-report/
e2e/.playwright/

# Python bytecode from the PreToolUse hooks. Machine-specific and rebuilt on
# every run; committing it puts a binary in every diff that touches a hook.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# F5 — verification output: test results, burn-in .trx files, drill logs,
# SBOMs and scan reports. Regenerated by `pnpm verify` on every run and
# uploaded by CI as build artifacts, so committing them would put megabytes
# of machine-specific output into every diff (8.5 MB after one local run).
_artifacts/

# `_workspace/` is deliberately NOT ignored. It holds the per-agent handoffs,
# and `scripts/certify-foundation.mjs` counts a missing handoff as a refusal
# — so ignoring it would make that gate permanently unsatisfiable on a fresh
# checkout, which is the opposite of what a certification gate is for.
